      "writtenOn": "2021-01-23T03:25:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think this is compatible with old designs, since this signal is disconnected and could swing low during RW runtime. We could add pull up.\n\nAlso, this means that new HW references running old RO could potentially go into low power idle.\n\nEither way we would need to spin a new RO for references that change this sleep line. I personally think we should remove the concept of low-power-idle and sleep lines from new ROs.\n\nhttps://github.com/coreboot/chrome-ec/blob/master/include/gpio.wrap#L153\nGPIO_INT_RO()",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 12,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 12,
        "endChar": 62
      },
      "revId": "3c20d3e104cda87a6769a5c9964d418d3aeb5195",
